    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideHeader">How to start mining: step-by-step guide</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideIntro">Follow these 5 steps in order, top to bottom. Each step matches one page in the menu on the left.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideStep1Header">1. GPU (graphics card)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideStep1Body">Open the "GPU" page. It shows how much video memory (VRAM) each of your cards has - you'll need that in step 4 to pick a model of the right size. For each card, choose a mode (easiest is to leave it on "Auto" - the app will pick what to run on it).</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideStep2Header">2. Node</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideStep2Body">Running your own node takes a long time to sync, so it's easier to start by connecting to someone else's public node. Open the "Node" page, click "Refresh list", pick a node from the list and click "Use" - the selected node will be highlighted so you can see which one is active. If you later want to run your own node, expand "My node settings" at the bottom of the same page and set the path to keryxd.exe and the connection address.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideStep3Header">3. Miner</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideStep3Body">Open the "Miner" page. Paste your reward address - this is your wallet, where mined coins will arrive. Turn on overheat protection and set the temperature thresholds (warning and critical) so your card doesn't overheat while mining.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideStep4Header">4. Models</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideStep4Body">Open the "Models" page. Each card shows how much VRAM that model needs - compare it with what you saw in step 1 and pick one that fits. Click "Download official model" - the easiest option, it downloads a verified version automatically (via torrent too, if that's faster). You can also get a model through Keryx Labs' Discord, where the team posts current mirrors - there's an "Open Discord" button on this same page. Wait until the progress bar reaches 100%.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideStep5Header">5. Start (Dashboard)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_About_GuideStep5Body">Go back to the Dashboard and click "Start All" - mining begins. If the status still shows "Stopped" even though the node or miner is clearly already running (e.g. you started it earlier), click "Refresh", or click "Stop All" once and then "Start All", so the app takes the processes back under its management.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_WindowTitle">Keryx Node Manager — First Run</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_HeaderTitle">Set up Keryx Node Manager</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step0_Title">Welcome</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step0_Body">This wizard will help you check your system once, set the paths to the node and miner, enter your reward address, and configure autostart. Everything can be changed later on the corresponding pages of the app — the wizard does not create a separate, independent configuration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step0_ActiveProfileLabel">The wizard is configuring profile:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step0_NewProfileHint">Setting up a second rig separately from the current profile? Create a new profile below — the wizard will switch to it immediately.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step0_NewProfileNamePlaceholder">New profile name</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step0_CreateProfile">Create and configure</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step1_Title">System check</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step1_Desc">Real checks are performed — Windows version, NVIDIA GPU presence (via nvidia-smi), WSL and Docker (optional).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step1_Updating">Updating...</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step1_WslDockerNote">WSL and Docker are not required — by default the app runs in native Windows mode.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step2_Title">Program and models folder paths</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step2_NodeLabel">keryxd.exe (node, optional at this step)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step2_MinerLabel">keryx-miner.exe (miner, optional at this step)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step2_ModelsLabel">Models folder (required)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step2_Browse">Browse...</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step2_Note">Paths to keryxd.exe/keryx-miner.exe can be set later on the "Node" and "Miner" pages — to continue the wizard, it's enough to set the models folder.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step2_NodeHeader">Node (keryxd.exe)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step2_MinerHeader">Miner (keryx-miner.exe)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step2_ModelsHeader">Models folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Wizard_Step2_ManualFileExpander">Specify a different file manually</sys:String>
