    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Node_FirewallExpanderHeader">Do I need to open a port and configure the firewall?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Node_FirewallBody1">No, not for mining. Your node works fine with an ordinary home internet connection and outgoing connections only - an open port/public IP is not needed for that.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Node_FirewallBody2">This is only needed if you WANT other network participants to be able to connect to your node (incoming connections) - this helps the health of the network as a whole, but isn't required for you personally. If you do want this: (1) you need a public IP address, not just one behind your provider's NAT/CGNAT; (2) you need to port-forward the node's P2P port (22111 by default) on your router to the computer running keryxd; (3) you need to allow inbound connections on that port for keryxd.exe in the Windows Firewall.</sys:String>
